// endpoint_get_run_settlements.proto — GetRunSettlements: WHICH of a set of
// detached runs the record already holds as ENDED.
//
// WHY THE SIDECAR ASKS. The sidecar's LOST policy tracks every detached run
// whose file it reads, and a run it saw settle (its spool's own terminator, the
// transcript's task notification, a person's stop, or a LOST conclusion) must
// never be tracked again. Knowing that a run settled used to live only in the
// sidecar's memory, so a restarted sidecar — which resumes each file at its
// committed cursor, PAST the terminator it already converted — re-tracked a
// finished run from its quiet file and later concluded it LOST, superseding
// the real terminal (2026-09-30, docs/protobuf-design/run-settlements.md). The
// settle is durable in exactly one place, the run's `detached_work` row, so
// that is what answers.
//
// UNSCOPED ON PURPOSE. The sidecar reads every session on the host; a run id is
// the spawning call's activity id and is compared for equality only.

